Ludwerk: a fragment density map on Vulkan, for a headset's foveated rendering.

SDL_GPU draws every pixel of a render pass at the same density. A headset
shades where the eye looks at full density and less towards the edges of
the lens, which on a phone's GPU is the largest saving a frame has; the
extension for it, VK_EXT_fragment_density_map, is a mobile GPU's. With this
patch the Vulkan backend enables the extension where the device has it
(its feature comes with it) and says, as device properties, how large an
area of a framebuffer a density texel covers. A texture made with
SDL_PROP_GPU_TEXTURE_CREATE_VULKAN_FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP_BOOLEAN is a
density map; a color target made with
SDL_PROP_GPU_TEXTURE_CREATE_VULKAN_DENSITY_MAP_POINTER names one, and a
render pass whose first color target it is carries that map as its
fragment density map attachment, in its layout for the pass and back
after it. A pipeline bound in such passes is made with
SDL_PROP_GPU_GRAPHICSPIPELINE_CREATE_VULKAN_FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP_BOOLEAN,
against a render pass with the same attachment. On a device without the
extension every property is ignored and nothing is drawn differently.
Upstream has no fragment density map; send it, or drop it when a pinned
release carries one.

